event: response.reasoning_summary_text.done
data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":95,"item_id":"rs_00f275ddf4fc8a41016ac8b87148148193a7357f554c11cdb2","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Considering SSR forms implementation**\n\nI'm thinking about implementing simple server-side rendered (SSR) forms that use client-side JavaScript for fetching submissions while handling alerts and redirects. I’ll make sure that the API POST route for projects returns JSON, while the UI can use native forms for submissions. I want to explore how to handle validation without relying purely on JavaScript, making it simpler for browsers with HTML, CSS, and necessary enhancements. I have ample time to test and validate the approach."}

